    {
      "id": "smart-charging",
      "title": "Smart Charging: The Intelligent Alternative",
      "narrative": "Instead of upgrading copper, we can use intelligence. Smart EV chargers receive signals from the network operator during peak periods. Cars that don't need immediate charging are automatically scheduled for later - during overnight low-demand hours. Owners barely notice: their car is still full by morning. The transformer stays within safe limits.",
