    {
      "id": "v2g-power",
      "title": "Vehicle-to-Grid: Cars as Batteries",
      "narrative": "Some EVs can do more than pause charging - they can export power back to the grid. During evening peak, V2G-enabled vehicles become distributed batteries, each contributing 5-10kW of export. Twelve V2G cars on Greenstead Road can provide 80kW of support during critical hours. That's like having a small battery storage facility, but using assets that already exist.",
