    {
      "id": "conclusion",
      "title": "The Future of Distribution",
      "narrative": "Flexibility represents a fundamental shift in how networks operate. Instead of building infrastructure for every peak, we can orchestrate demand and distributed resources to use existing assets more efficiently. EVs, batteries, heat pumps - they're not just loads, they're partners in running a smarter grid. This is how we enable Net Zero without gold-plating the network.",
